---
title: "Herdr restart B ports: owned idle recovery, existing operation ticket, effect permission"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Result
    lg1: Restart
    lg2: Breaks NoSeedAfterClear
    lg3: Breaks NoResumeAfterClear in some cases
    lg4: Path to the ClearForgets or NoResumeAfterClear or NoSeedAfterClear bug
    lg5: Repeats forever, so ClearForgets breaks
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 mayBreak
  class lg4 bugPath
  class lg5 repeats
  s0: Old session and a queued input
  s1: Seed committed#59; gate holds it
  s2: Restart holds the transition and fence
  s3: Exact close confirmed#59; retire and settle
  s4: Old execution retired#59; exclusion still held
  s5: Clear requested#59; epoch serializer pending
  s6: Clear began: epoch bumped#59; restart holds the transition
  s7: Clear began: epoch bumped#59; no session
  s8: Clear discarded the queue#59; restart holds the transition
  s9: A launch resumed the conversation a clear ended
  s10: Old execution retired#59; a clear overtook the restart
  s11: Exclusion released#59; superseded reply pending
  s12: Clear gave up on the transition#59; selector still kept
  s13: The seed ran after a clear began
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: Commit the seed original (acceptance)
  s1 --> s2: Terminate takes transition and fence
  s2 --> s3: Close only the captured pane
  s3 --> s4: Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s3 --> s5: User requests clear
  s4 --> s5: User requests clear
  s5 --> s5: Accept an input into the owner queue
  s5 --> s6: Acquire the serializer and bump the clear epoch
  s6 --> s7: Clear epoch ignored: selector kept
  s6 --> s8: Clear discards the queue and the launching input
  s7 --> s9: Owner starts the front: register the launch
  s8 --> s3: Clear's teardown acts on the row
  s9 --> s9: Install Pending over the vacant row or Observe the create epoch or Compare live epoch and retain create permission or Create once under live effect permission or Observe the input epoch or Compare live epoch and retain input permission
  s3 --> s10: Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s10 --> s11: Clear epoch ignored: selector kept
  s11 --> s12: Reply to the command
  s9 --> s13: Submit the first input under live permission
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
